Version 1.0.0 - Sep 12 2026
* Complete migration from KDE 2/3 + Qt3 to native Qt6 (QApplication,
  QMainWindow, QSerialPort/QSerialPortInfo replace all KDE Frameworks
  and the raw POSIX/termios serial backend); CMake build system
  replaces the old Autotools/KDevelop-1.2 setup. Renamed to
  Komport-Qt6 as an independent continuation - the original "Komport"
  (Mike Sharkey, last active 2003) is no longer maintained upstream.
* Terminal emulation: broader VT100/VT102 coverage (cursor counters,
  insert/delete line/char, DECCKM/DECTCEM, device status reports),
  VT220/xterm extensions (256-color SGR, scroll regions/DECSTBM,
  insert mode).
* Admin/diagnosis tooling: toggleable RX/TX hex monitor, programmable
  macro bar, one-click session logging, line-ending selection
  (CR/LF/CRLF), device profiles (serial parameters + line ending +
  macro bar bundled per profile, with ready-made Cisco/HP/Aruba
  presets).
* Appearance tab: font family/spacing, custom or preset color schemes
  (Breeze Light/Dark, Green-on-Black, Amber).
* Retro/industrial character-set translation (CP437, PETSCII built
  in) between the raw serial byte stream and the terminal display,
  plus user-defined *.charset files (no code/rebuild needed).
* Internationalization: full Qt6 Linguist infrastructure, all visible
  UI strings translatable. Ships with all 24 EU official languages
  (23 fully translated, Irish intentionally left untranslated pending
  further review) plus Russian; falls back cleanly to English for any
  unfinished string or unsupported locale.
* Extensive regression test suite (Qt6::Test, run via ctest) covering
  crash classes found across multiple rounds of adversarial code
  review (profile/array-size validation, unbounded escape-sequence
  buffers, window/serial-port lifetime, cell-array bounds, i18n data
  integrity).
* Full history of the migration, every review round and its findings:
  see TODO-ARCHIVE.md. Known, deliberately accepted gaps: see TODO.md.

